      "writtenOn": "2026-04-13T18:59:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m curious, what is the motivation for this kind of changes? A lot of these assertions should be programmer errors. i.e. there shouldn\u0027t be a way for the external users to abuse them.\n\nLike this commandContext. An external user cannot allocate it. It can only be allocated by the internal code itself. If it\u0027s null, it is the bug in the internal code. Why do we have to change to runtime checks?\n\nI\u0027m not comfortable changing too many assertions to runtime checks. Graphite/Dawn already has higher CPU overheads compared to Ganesh in many cases and we want to reduce it as much as possible. I think a tests on motionmark on Mac doesn\u0027t represent all the real-world use cases and different kinds of hardwares.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1147,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1147,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "70de7b5d2a0b1b63dab2f3de58533fb74a58302e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5b7127e_bd86a2be",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BufferD3D11.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 1147,
      "author": {
        "id": 3461520
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-13T19:22:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do have other tests (graphite skia) that will check if we make major regressions.\n\nThe motivation here is of course security.  There are examples of security bugs that would have been caught if only we had hit asserts at runtime.\n\nAs for cost. Checks that are null or bounding are basically free unless they are in extreme tight loops. They only cost a cmp and a predicted branch. In cases where they would be hot we should not add them. This is why i have not converted all asserts but a subset of them.",
      "parentUuid": "4f7e021e_539eef7e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1147,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1147,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "70de7b5d2a0b1b63dab2f3de58533fb74a58302e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
